infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title Pluggable CC covers the full deployment spectrum
  desc Four algorithms, four niches — swappable per connection in user space, no kernel patch
  lists
    - label NewReno — the safe default
      desc RFC 9002 baseline: slow start, additive increase, halve cwnd on loss. The conservative fallback every QUIC stack must support.
    - label CUBIC — aggressive LAN probing
      desc Cloudflare quiche default and the Linux kernel standard. A cubic function reprobes hard after loss, winning on low-RTT high-bandwidth paths.
    - label BBR — high-throughput WAN
      desc Google YouTube and Cloudflare edges. Models bottleneck bandwidth and minimum RTT, ignoring random loss that would collapse CUBIC.
    - label HyStart++ — exit slow start early
      desc Paired with CUBIC: detects queueing build-up to leave slow start before overshoot, trimming startup loss.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #8b5cf6
